    {
      "id": 161,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -1860,
        5960
      ],
      "size": [
        700,
        260
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 10,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# (cut plan variant) H3 Music Video\n\n1. **Load the song** → `audio` of the **H3 Music Video Writer** (and `replace_audio` of H3 Scenes Join, so the finished video carries the original track).\n2. The writer cuts the song into 5–15 s pieces on the music (timed lyrics make cuts land before lines), writes one scene per piece with `<Audio 1>` = that piece, and emits matching lists: `scenes` → prompt, `lengths` → length (frame counts on H3's grid), `audio_segments` → `ref_audio_1`.\n3. The H3 video node runs once per piece and each clip is DECODED AND SAVED as its own video file (VAE Decode → Create Video → Save Video). Stitch externally, or re-add **H3 Scenes Join** before Create Video for one file with the original song.\n\nPut lyrics with timestamps (`[0:12] line`) for exact lip-sync; a custom performer + wardrobe comes from the H3 Characters node (✏️ custom). Connect reference images (the performer's face) to the writer's `image_1..` and they reach the video node and the preview thumbnails.\n\n**Seed:** the writer's seed is **-1 (randomize)** - every queue writes a brand-new video; nothing is reused from earlier runs. To use the Review node's stop-edit-**Continue** flow, first set the writer's seed to a FIXED number: Continue relies on ComfyUI reusing the cached scenes, and with -1 each queue writes fresh scenes and re-reviews instead.\n\n**Original sound:** every saved clip carries its ORIGINAL slice of the song (the writer's `audio_segments`, cut on the same frame grid) - not the model-generated audio, and in the masked workflow not the vocals-only stem. Wire Create Video's `audio` back to VAE Decode Audio if you want to hear what the model generated."
      ],
      "title": "How this works",
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    },
