    {
      "id": 205,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -1860,
        6290
      ],
      "size": [
        400,
        360
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 0,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Beat sync",
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Beat sync\n\n**Beat Grid** measures the tempo and lists every beat (phase fitted to Sound Events' hits).\n\n**Cut Plan** with `beat_snap` moves every cut onto the nearest beat, frame-exact - so every scene OPENS on the beat. The writer keeps those exact lengths (it says so in its log) and each piece's brief lists `[beat] every 0.469 s at +0.00 +0.47 ...` so the model times the action to the pulse. Only **Chain Render** can use this: it renders the next 17-frame length up and trims the pad.\n\n**Beat Emphasis** is **bypassed** in this workflow: with it on, H3 listened to a thump on every beat mixed over the voice instead of the music - the motion went jittery and stopped following the song, and the cut-before-every-lyric-line plan put no cut on a drop. Now the Cut Plan cuts **on the music** (Auto: onsets / drops / sections, still snapped to the beat) and Chain Render is conditioned on the plain **vocal stem**, like the masked-audio workflow. Un-bypass the node to A/B it. When on, it takes the **vocal stem** (not the song) and lays a thump on every beat with a small spike (`boost_db` 3, `duck_db` 0) - wired into Chain Render's `conditioning_audio`, it is what H3 *listens* to while the original song still goes to the output. The vocal stem is what the lips follow; the thumps are the beat cue. Feeding the full mix here, spiked +9 dB and ducked -6 dB, buries the voice and the lip-sync goes with it. Whether the picture follows the beat more tightly is an experiment: render with and without, run **Sync Check** on both.\n\nSound Events' `on_beat_weight` (and its 🎚 editor's Signal section: gain / curve / EQ) shapes which hits count as beats in the first place.\n\n**Voice Over Music** is what Chain Render listens to now (`conditioning_audio`): the Vocals stem at full level with Drums + Bass + Other summed **-9 dB** under it, ducked a further **-6 dB** only while the voice sounds. The mouth follows the voice, the picture moves on the real beat, and no word is buried. `music_db` is the dial: -3 is nearly the full song, -18 is a whisper of beat. The bypassed Beat Emphasis sits after it, so un-bypassing adds thumps on top of this mix for an A/B."
      ]
    },
